pulation is would be maybe  welcoming russian of troops moving in  and  the the majority would not  so that means the russian military i  believe if they move in they're going to  try to  limit that to those areas of ukraine  which are russian speaking and where  they would accept expect at least some  more friendly  populations than in other parts  mr felgenhauer joining us tonight from  moscow we appreciate your time and your  insights tonight thank you  thank you  a few minutes ago  i have welcomed the first soldiers of  our reinforcement forces it's a strong  signal that germany is willing and  capable to reinforce the battle group  immediately if needed  and within the next few days  i expect around 350 additional soldiers  and around 100 additional vehicles  that was the commander of german forces  in lithuania 350 additional german  troops have arrived in the country to  shore up nato's eastern flank now they  are the first contingent of  reinforcements  as you heard more troops and vehicles  are expected to arrive in the coming  days lithuania following the african  country mali  is now home to the second largest  foreign deployment of german forces  the soldiers form part of a nato battle  group which is designed to delay an  attack by  russia in the baltics and to buy time  for additional troops to reach  the front  lines  well our correspondent jack parrok he is  in vilnius lithuania for us tonight good  evening to you  jack so let's talk about what we're  seeing here 350 additional german troops  with more on the way  is this enough to deter the russians  from any military action  against the baltic states or is this  more symbolism  well it's certainly a symbolism but it  is also significant what we heard during  that press conference at kaunas airport  earlier where the first 70 of the  additional 350 troops were arriving  is that there will be not only artillery  soldiers not only recce reconnaissance  specialists and medics but also  interestingly that there will be  specialists in nuclear and biological  warfare that will be deployed into this  battle group these 350 extra takes the  troop numbers to somewhere near 1500  here in lithuania as part of that battle  group coordinated by nato and run by  the german commander there and  essentially what they're saying is that  they're trying to beef up they're trying  to be prepared they don't say that they  have any warnings necessarily of any  potential uh invasions into lithuania by  the russians but with everything going  on on the on the border there is a sense  here that this was this was something  that germany you know could do in order  to show support for the baltic nations  who've been  really concerned about everything that's  going on in ukraine for their own safety  as well  let's stay with that for a moment  jack i mean we are talking  almost non-stop about  the russian threat along the border  with ukraine  but a little further north  these baltic states you know they also  have russia as a neighbor i mean are  they worried that the russian threat  could soon be much greater than it is  now  they certainly are the government has  been raising alarm bells here in  lithuania the latvians the estonians the  poles as well have very similar concerns  all ex-soviet states and  while there wasn't quite the scenes uh  like we're seeing now in ukraine all of  these countries still have a huge  hangover and a lot of a fear of what  moscow could potentially do many people  here remember living under  under the soviet union and they're aware  of you know the fear of that potentially  maybe returning having said that i've  spoken to to younger people here on the  streets of vilnius and earlier in  calmness as well and there's an acute  concern among the younger generations  who perhaps didn't live under the soviet  union themselves  they are pretty pleased that these new  german troops have arrived a lot of  people we've spoken to say good yeah we  should get som